### Demo-only secrets & generated certs/keystores ###
# Self-signed dev TLS cert - regenerable per-environment, never meant to be
# shared between machines, never committed even though a working demo
# needs it to exist locally - see the top-level demo repo's README for how
# it gets (re)generated on first run.
#
# docker-compose/verifier-backend/verifier-access.p12 is deliberately NOT
# listed here (it used to be, incorrectly - copy-pasted from this same
# pattern without noticing it's a different kind of file): unlike the TLS
# cert above, it's a static, hash-pinned demo credential, not something
# regenerated per environment - VERIFIER_ORIGINALCLIENTID in
# docker-compose.yaml hardcodes its SHA-256 hash, so a fresh clone with no
# committed .p12 (or a freshly-regenerated one with a different hash)
# breaks verifier-backend outright at startup. It's committed, same as the
# issuer's own equally-static issuer-keys.jks already was.
docker-compose/haproxy/certs/*
src/main/resources/*.jks
!docker-compose/haproxy/certs/.gitkeep
# Stamp file for the top-level Makefile's incremental image-build tracking
.image-built
